<%# workspace-main.ejs
     What an in-app navigation actually sends.

     The shell — topbar, sidebar, theme, command dialog, the countdown —
     is already in the browser and already correct. Re-sending it on every
     tab change means the browser throws away a working header and rebuilds
     an identical one, which is where the flicker on /wire -> /watches came
     from. So this is the contents of <main> and nothing else.

     The <title> must be a DIRECT child here: htmx lifts a top-level title
     out of a fragment and puts it on the document. Nested inside anything
     it is ignored, and the tab would keep the previous page's name. %>
<title><%= title %> · Job Wire</title>
<%- include('../partials/workspace-heading') %>
<%- body %>
